<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Trading in line with the close.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Trading in line with the close.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading activity was light after hours, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;I really do not see things trading away from where they closed,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said GRC International Inc, Lukens Inc, J. Ray McDermott, McDermott International Inc, Advanced Micro Devices Inc and Fruehauf Trailer Corp were not available for after hours trade.  </p>
<p>The NYSE said session one volume was 1,100 shares, compared to 59,500 shares Friday. Session two volume was 1,141,068 shares versus none Friday.</p>
<p>The American Stock Exchange said there was no after-hours activity.</p>
</text>
